Problem1:
Write DArray class, both specification and implementation. The DArray class represents a type that mimics an array that changes its size dynamically. The DArray class shall be such that the following main(…) program executes correctly.
 
int main(){
    DArray darr1, darr2;			//darr1 & darr2 have size 0
    for (int j{}; j < 15; ++j){
    	darr1.push_back(j*2);
    }
    cout << darr1 << endl;
    darr2 = darr1;
    for (int j{15}; j >= 0; --j){
    	darr2.push_back(j*3);
    }
    cout << darr2 << endl;

    return 0;
} 

(Note: Write only the required functions. No extra function is allowed.)

